<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns:ns1="http://purl.org/hitop#0004" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:obo="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:iao="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao">
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01i7x">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Pain =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by the subjective experience of physical discomfort or distress, 
            which may vary in intensity, duration, and localization.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait characterized by the subjective experience of physical discomfort or distress, which may vary in intensity, duration, and localization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pain</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U0036N">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Fear =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by emotional responses to perceived threats or danger, 
            typically involving heightened arousal, avoidance behaviors, and anticipatory anxiety.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear refers to an emotional response to perceived threats or danger.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fear</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00fKQ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Generalized Anxiety Disorder Symptoms =def. a Distress which is characterized by excessive and persistent worry 
            that interferes with daily functioning, often accompanied by physical symptoms such as restlessness, fatigue, 
            and muscle tension.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component of generalized anxiety disorder symptoms is excessive, persistent worry that interferes with daily life and is often accompanied by physical symptoms like restlessness and fatigue.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Generalized anxiety disorder symptoms</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P006gM">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Antagonistic Externalizing =def. an Externalizing which is characterized by hostile and 
            aggressive behaviors directed toward others, reflecting interpersonal antagonism and a tendency 
            to violate social norms or the rights of others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Antagonistic Externalizing describes behaviors that involve hostility and aggression towards others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Antagonistic Externalizing</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum is designed to accommodate potential future modifications and expansions. 
            It supports the integration of new spectra or related concepts to reflect advancements in understanding antagonistic externalizing behaviors and their classification.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#S0013h">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Externalizing =def. a General Psychopathology which is characterized by outwardly directed behaviors and 
            dysregulation, including impulsivity, aggression, and rule-breaking actions that disrupt external environments.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Represents a broad HiTOP dimension characterized by outwardly directed behaviors and dysregulation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Externalizing</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This superspectrum is structured to support future refinements and extensions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of additional spectra or subdimensions to reflect ongoing developments 
            in the conceptualization and classification of externalizing behaviors and dysregulation.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00XyI">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Anhedonia =def. a Distress which is conceptualized as a transient reduction in the capacity to experience pleasure, 
            often emerging in response to acute stress or mood states, leading to a temporary inability to enjoy previously pleasurable activities.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Anhedonia conceptualized as a Component refers to a transient reduction in the capacity to experience pleasure, often emerging in response to acute stress or mood states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anhedonia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00pnZ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Reckless Overconfidence =def. a Mania which is characterized by excessive self-confidence that leads to risky, 
            impulsive, or poorly judged behaviors, often without regard for potential negative consequences, as 
            commonly observed in manic episodes.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Excessive self-confidence leading to risky or impulsive behavior, often seen in manic episodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Reckless overconfidence</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01XQi">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Attention Seeking =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a constant need for validation 
            or recognition, often leading to behaviors aimed at drawing focus from others, typically through exaggerated actions, 
            statements, or displays.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait of attention seeking is the constant need for validation or recognition, often leading to behavior aimed at drawing focus from others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Attention seeking</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C021Q0">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Low orgasmic function =def. a Sexual problems component characterized by diminished ability, frequency, or 
            satisfaction in reaching orgasm, often associated with sexual dysfunction.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by diminished ability, frequency, or satisfaction in reaching orgasm, often associated with sexual dysfunction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Low orgasmic function</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C02BO8">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Inattention =def. a Disinhibition component defined by difficulties sustaining focus, being easily distracted, 
            or failing to maintain attention during tasks or activities.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component defined by difficulties sustaining focus, being easily distracted, or failing to maintain attention during tasks or activities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Inattention</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T008mD">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Emotional Lability =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by rapid and intense emotional changes, often leading 
            to unpredictable shifts in mood, ranging from euphoria to sadness, with difficulty in regulating emotional responses.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by rapid and intense emotional changes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Emotional lability</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P004R1">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Detachment =def. a General Psychopathology which is characterized by emotional distance and disengagement 
            from social interactions, reflecting a reduced capacity for affective connection and interpersonal involvement.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Detachment refers to a psychological state characterized by emotional distance and disengagement from social interactions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Detachment</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum is designed to accommodate the inclusion of new related spectra or additional concepts as understanding of detachment and related psychological phenomena evolves. 
            It supports updates and extensions to reflect advances in research and shifts in diagnostic criteria.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00S9m">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Cleaning =def. a Fear which is characterized by compulsive behaviors related to cleaning or hygiene, 
            typically performed to reduce anxiety about contamination or illness.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Compulsive behaviors related to cleaning or hygiene.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cleaning</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00iAh">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Hyperarousal =def. a Distress which is characterized by increased physiological arousal, including symptoms such as 
            hypervigilance, irritability, exaggerated startle response, and difficulty sleeping, often associated with 
            trauma-related or anxiety disorders.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Increased physiological arousal, including symptoms such as hypervigilance, irritability, and difficulty sleeping.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hyperarousal</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00RGy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Psychological Panic =def. a Fear which is characterized by an intense and overwhelming sense of fear accompanied 
            by cognitive symptoms such as a perceived loss of control, fear of going crazy, or impending doom, 
            often triggering physical reactions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component of psychological panic is an intense, overwhelming fear that triggers physical symptoms and a sense of losing control.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Psychological panic</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00G3d">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Fragility =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a lack of resilience and a tendency to be easily hurt or 
            affected by stress, often leading to emotional instability or difficulty coping with adversity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of resilience and a tendency to be easily hurt or affected by stress.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fragility</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00ua9">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Eccentricity =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by unconventional or peculiar behavior, 
            including odd mannerisms, unusual beliefs, or idiosyncratic ways of interacting with others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by unconventional or peculiar behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Eccentricity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01UGN">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Rebelliousness =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by resistance to authority, rules, and 
            societal norms, often manifested through defiance, disobedience, or challenging established systems or conventions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by resistance to authority and norms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rebelliousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00l5y">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Irritability =def. a Distress which is characterized by a heightened tendency to become easily annoyed or angered, 
            often involving a low tolerance for frustration and frequent mood outbursts.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">State of being easily annoyed or angered, often with a low tolerance for frustration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Irritability</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01RYG">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Boredom Proneness =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a tendency to experience boredom frequently 
            and easily, often leading to restlessness, dissatisfaction, and a search for novel or stimulating experiences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait indicating a tendency to experience boredom frequently and easily.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Boredom proneness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C005Sv">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Gastrointestinal =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by gastrointestinal symptoms such as abdominal pain, 
            bloating, nausea, or altered bowel habits that cannot be fully explained by medical findings, 
            reflecting psychological distress expressed through digestive complaints.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component related to gastrointestinal symptoms and disorders.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gastrointestinal</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00Y8j">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Insomnia =def. a Distress which is characterized by difficulty falling asleep, staying asleep, or waking too 
            early and being unable to return to sleep, often resulting in daytime fatigue, irritability, or impaired functioning.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Difficulty falling asleep or staying asleep, or waking up too early and not being able to go back to sleep.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Insomnia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop">
    <iao:IAO_0000115 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iao.owl"/>
    <dcterms:contributor>Dr. Rogério Blitz</dcterms:contributor>
