    <rdfs:label>Hierarchical Taxonomy of Psychopathology (HiTOP) Ontology</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>This ontology implements a structured representation of the Hierarchical Taxonomy of Psychopathology (HiTOP) and is designed to support an open, extensible framework for modeling mental health dimensions. It allows for the representation of an unlimited number of factor structures and variants, enabling flexible integration of empirical findings and theoretical refinements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.hitop-system.org/"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>0.1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <skos:changeNote rdf:resource="https://www.w3.org/2009/08/skos-reference/skos.html"/>
    <dc:title xml:lang="en">Hierarchical Taxonomy of Psychopathology (HiTOP) Ontology</dc:title>
    <dc:description xml:lang="en">Implements a structured representation of the Hierarchical Taxonomy of Psychopathology (HiTOP) for modeling mental health dimensions, factor structures, and taxonomy variants.</dc:description>
    <dc:license rdf:resource="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"/>
  </owl:Ontology>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T014BA">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Attention Seeking =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a reduced or absent desire to attract and hold 
            the attention of others, often reflecting low social expressiveness or a preference for remaining unnoticed in 
            social settings.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by limited motivation to attract, maintain, or enhance the attention of others, often manifested as reduced social display, self-promotion, or efforts to gain recognition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Attention seeking</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#F001Hw">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            General Psychopathology = Def. a Psychological Condition which manifests across multiple 
            mental health disorders and includes broad symptoms such as mood disturbances, anxiety, 
            cognitive dysfunctions, and behavioral problems.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">General Psychopathology refers to the broad, overarching category of mental disorders and psychological symptoms that can manifest across different mental health conditions. It encompasses a wide range of psychological phenomena that are not specific to any single disorder but may contribute to or exacerbate multiple types of mental health issues. This category includes general symptoms and traits that are commonly observed in various psychiatric conditions, such as mood disturbances, anxiety, cognitive dysfunctions, and behavioral problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">General Psychopathology</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote>
            Indicates the potential for future inclusion of additional spectra and other related concepts as new developments and 
            insights emerge in the field of general psychopathology. Allows for flexible expansion and refinement of the taxonomy 
            to integrate new spectra, subfactors, and related elements to better capture evolving understanding and research 
            findings.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01VXq">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Empathy =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a reduced ability to understand and 
            share the feelings of others, often leading to emotional detachment, indifference, or difficulty in 
            forming meaningful interpersonal connections.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait indicating a reduced ability to understand and share the feelings of others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Empathy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C001qy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Conversion =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by the expression of psychological distress as neurological or 
            physical symptoms that are inconsistent with medical findings, reflecting unconscious processes underlying the 
            symptom presentation.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component related to conversion disorders where psychological distress is expressed as physical symptoms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Conversion</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T013F1">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Disaffiliativeness =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a lack of interest in forming or maintaining 
            social bonds, often reflecting indifference toward closeness, companionship, or interpersonal connection.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of interest in forming or maintaining social bonds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Disaffiliativeness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P005xY">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Disinhibited Externalizing =def. an Externalizing which is characterized by impulsive behaviors and 
            a lack of social restraint or inhibition, reflecting difficulties in self-regulation and behavioral control.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Disinhibited Externalizing involves behaviors that are impulsive and lacking in social restraint or inhibition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Disinhibited Externalizing</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum is designed to be adaptable to the addition of new spectra or related concepts as research on disinhibited externalizing behaviors evolves. 
            It allows for updates and expansions to incorporate emerging findings and shifts in diagnostic frameworks.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00LqY">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Public Places =def. a Fear which is characterized by fear or anxiety associated with being in public spaces, 
            often involving concern about escape or access to help in case of distress.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear or anxiety associated with being in public spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Public places</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00IAT">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Invulnerability =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a perception of being immune to harm or 
            negative effects, often leading to risky behavior, overconfidence, or a lack of consideration for potential consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a perception of being immune to harm or negative effects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Invulnerability</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00zDk">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Intimacy Avoidance =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a tendency to avoid close relationships and 
            emotional intimacy, often due to discomfort with closeness, fear of vulnerability, or preference for emotional distance.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to avoid close relationships and emotional intimacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Intimacy avoidance</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01C1W">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Workaholism =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing trait characterized by a reduced tendency toward excessive and compulsive involvement in work, resulting in less interference with personal wellbeing, relationships, and leisure time.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by reduced levels of excessive and compulsive commitment to work, with less impact on personal well-being and relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Workaholism</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00xLn">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Fantasy Proneness =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by a tendency to engage in vivid and complex 
            fantasies, often involving imaginative immersion, daydreaming, or blurred boundaries between imagination and reality.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to engage in vivid and complex fantasies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fantasy proneness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#V106mv">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#0004KV"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The HiTOP Emotional Dysfunction Ontology version 1.0 formalizes the superspectrum of emotional experience and regulation. It encodes components, traits, and subdimensions related to heightened negative affect, diminished positive affect, and difficulties in managing or expressing emotions, supporting dimensional and hierarchical representation for research and clinical applications.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-30</dcterms:issued>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HiTOP Emotional dysfunction Ontology Version 1.0</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </owl:NamedIndividual>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00Pjp">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Blood-Injection-Injury =def. a Fear which is characterized by fear or anxiety related to blood, injections, 
            or injuries, often accompanied by physiological responses such as fainting or nausea and resulting in 
            avoidance of medical procedures or traumatic stimuli.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear or anxiety related to blood, injections, or injuries.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Blood-injection-injury</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C024WG">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Physiological anxiety =def. a Somatoform and Distress component reflecting bodily manifestations of anxiety such 
            as rapid heartbeat, sweating, trembling, or gastrointestinal discomfort.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component reflecting bodily manifestations of anxiety such as rapid heartbeat, sweating, trembling, or gastrointestinal discomfort.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Physiological anxiety</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T016k0">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Irresponsibility =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by a lack of regard for the consequences 
            of one’s actions, often leading to reckless, careless, or socially inappropriate behaviors.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of regard for the consequences of one's actions, often leading to reckless behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Irresponsibility</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01pc6">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Anxiety sensitivity =def. a Fear trait which is defined by the fear of anxiety-related sensations, based on beliefs 
            that these sensations have harmful physical, psychological, or social consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting the fear of anxiety-related sensations, based on beliefs that these sensations have harmful physical, psychological, or social consequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anxiety sensitivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00bEx">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Retardation =def. a Distress which is characterized by slowed cognitive and physical processes, including delays 
            in thinking, speaking, and moving, often observed in depressive states.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Slowed cognitive and physical processes, including thinking, speaking, and moving.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Retardation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01kKJ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Neurological =def. a Somatoform which is defined by functional disturbances or symptoms related to the nervous system, 
            including sensory, motor, or cognitive manifestations.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait reflecting functional disturbances or symptoms related to the nervous system, including sensory, motor, or cognitive manifestations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Neurological</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00VHv">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Dysphoria =def. a Distress which is characterized by a generalized state of unhappiness, dissatisfaction, 
            or emotional discomfort, often involving irritability, restlessness, or low mood without a specific cause.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state of generalized unhappiness or dissatisfaction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dysphoria</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01A5i">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Rigid Perfectionism =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing trait characterized by a reduced tendency to strive for perfection and inflexible high standards, often associated with greater tolerance of imperfections and increased adaptability to mistakes or setbacks.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a low tendency toward excessive and inflexible striving for perfection and high standards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Rigid perfectionism</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#S003TB">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Psychosis =def. a General Psychopathology superspectrum encompassing disturbances in reality testing and self-experience, 
            including abnormalities of perception, belief, and thought such as hallucinations, delusions, disorganization, and related negative symptoms (e.g., avolition, blunted affect).
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A superspectrum encompassing disturbances in reality testing and self-experience, including abnormalities of perception, belief, and thought such as hallucinations, delusions, disorganization, and related negative symptoms (e.g., avolition, blunted affect).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Psychosis</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This superspectrum is designed to accommodate future refinements and extensions. 
            It enables the addition of further components or subdimensions to capture evolving understanding 
            of disturbances in reality testing, perception, belief, and related negative symptoms.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C0237W">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Decreased need for sleep =def. a Mania component or trait marked by a reduced requirement for sleep without a 
            corresponding sense of fatigue, often associated with altered mood or energy states.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait marked by a reduced requirement for sleep without a corresponding sense of fatigue, often associated with altered mood or energy states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Decreased need for sleep</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T02A06">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Romantic disinterest =def. a Detachment trait marked by diminished or absent interest in forming or maintaining 
            romantic relationships, independent of sexual orientation or activity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait marked by diminished or absent interest in forming or maintaining romantic relationships, independent of sexual orientation or activity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Romantic disinterest</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#V108kx">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#0004KV"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The HiTOP Externalizing Ontology version 1.0 formalizes the superspectrum of outwardly directed behaviors and dysregulation. It encodes components, traits, and subdimensions related to aggression, impulsivity, and rule-breaking, supporting dimensional and hierarchical representation for research and clinical applications.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-30</dcterms:issued>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HiTOP Externalizing Ontology Version 1.0</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </owl:NamedIndividual>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01ueZ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Purging =def. an Eating pathology component which is defined by recurrent compensatory behaviors such as self-induced 
            vomiting, misuse of laxatives, or diuretics aimed at preventing weight gain after eating.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component involving recurrent compensatory behaviors such as self-induced vomiting, misuse of laxatives, or diuretics aimed at preventing weight gain after eating.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Purging</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T026cQ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Peculiarity =def. a Thought disorder trait characterized by unusual, unconventional, or idiosyncratic patterns of 
            thinking, perception, or behavior that deviate from social norms.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by unusual, unconventional, or idiosyncratic patterns of thinking, perception, or behavior that deviate from social norms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Peculiarity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U0012Y">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Sexual Problems =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by difficulties and dysfunctions related
            to sexual health and behavior, reflecting internal psychological distress that manifests in sexual functioning.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Sexual Problems encompass difficulties and dysfunctions related to sexual health and behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sexual Problems</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T029jr">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Social withdrawal =def. a Detachment trait defined by the tendency to avoid or disengage from social interactions 
            and relationships, often leading to reduced social contact and support.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait defined by the tendency to avoid or disengage from social interactions and relationships, often leading to reduced social contact and support.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Social withdrawal</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00Eht">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Identity Problems =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by difficulties in forming or maintaining a stable sense of 
            self, often resulting in confusion about one's values, goals, or role in life, and leading to instability in 
            personal identity or self-concept.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by difficulties in forming or maintaining a stable sense of self.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Identity problems</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01rfi">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Body dissatisfaction =def. an Eating pathology component or trait which is defined by persistent negative evaluations 
            of one’s own body shape, weight, or appearance, often linked to distress and maladaptive behaviors.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait defined by persistent negative evaluations of one’s own body shape, weight, or appearance, often linked to distress and maladaptive behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Body dissatisfaction</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P002nf">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Internalizing =def. a General Psychopathology which is characterized by inward-directed symptoms such as anxiety, 
            depression, and social withdrawal, indicating emotional and cognitive distress that is primarily internal in nature.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Internalizing label refers to a category of mental health disorders characterized by inward-focused symptoms such as anxiety, depression, and withdrawal, reflecting emotional and cognitive distress.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Internalizing</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum can accommodate future additions or modifications based on emerging research or evolving understanding of internalizing disorders. 
            It is designed to integrate new related spectra or concepts as needed, reflecting the ongoing developments in the field.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01mPz">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Negative emotionality =def. a Distress trait which is defined by a general tendency to experience frequent and 
            intense negative emotions such as sadness, anxiety, and guilt across diverse situations.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting a general tendency to experience frequent and intense negative emotions such as sadness, anxiety, and guilt across diverse situations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Negative emotionality</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U0050q">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Mania =def. an Internalizing and Thought Disorder which is characterized by elevated mood, 
            increased activity levels, and impulsive behavior, reflecting dysregulation in affective and cognitive functioning.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Mania is characterized by elevated mood, increased activity, and impulsive behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mania</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01Y7w">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Callousness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a lack of empathy and 
            a tendency to be emotionally cold or indifferent to others, often resulting in a disregard for the feelings 
            or well-being of others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of empathy and a tendency to be emotionally cold or indifferent to others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Callousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01cX5">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Rudeness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a lack of manners or 
            respect in social interactions, often involving offensive or inappropriate behaviors that disregard social norms 
            and conventions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of manners or respect in social interactions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rudeness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U002SC">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Eating Pathology =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by disordered eating behaviors and 
            maladaptive concerns related to body image, reflecting internal psychological distress expressed through eating 
            and self-perception.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Eating Pathology includes disorders and maladaptive behaviors related to eating and body image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Eating Pathology</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#V10749">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#0004KV"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The HiTOP Psychosis Ontology version 1.0 formalizes the superspectrum encompassing disturbances in reality testing, perception, belief, and thought. It encodes components, traits, and related negative symptoms, enabling dimensional and hierarchical representation of psychotic experiences for clinical and research purposes.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-30</dcterms:issued>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HiTOP Psychosis Ontology Version 1.0</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </owl:NamedIndividual>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T015o8">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Problematic Impulsivity =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by difficulty in controlling 
            impulsive behaviors, often resulting in actions that lead to negative consequences for oneself or others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by difficulty in controlling impulsive behaviors, often leading to negative consequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Problematic impulsivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#S002SE">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Emotional dysfunction =def. a General Psychopathology superspectrum encompassing a broad range of disturbances in 
            emotional experience and regulation, including heightened negative affect, diminished positive affect, and difficulties in managing or expressing emotions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A superspectrum encompassing a broad range of disturbances in emotional experience and regulation, including heightened negative affect, diminished positive affect, and difficulties in managing or expressing emotions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Emotional dysfunction</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This superspectrum is structured to support ongoing refinements and extensions. 
            It allows for incorporation of additional components or subdimensions to reflect advances 
            in the conceptualization and classification of emotional experience and regulatory difficulties.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U0061L">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Harmful Substance Abuse =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by excessive use of substances 
            that leads to significant harm or impairment in physical, psychological, or social functioning.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Harmful Substance Abuse refers to the excessive use of substances that causes significant harm or impairment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Harmful Substance Abuse</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00Q1t">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Physiological Panic =def. a Fear which is characterized by sudden episodes of intense anxiety accompanied by 
            physiological symptoms such as rapid heartbeat, sweating, shortness of breath, or dizziness, 
            reflecting acute autonomic arousal.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Panic attacks characterized by physiological symptoms such as rapid heartbeat and sweating.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Physiological panic</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01s9T">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Binge eating =def. an Eating pathology component which is defined by recurrent episodes of consuming unusually 
            large amounts of food, accompanied by a sense of loss of control during the episode.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by recurrent episodes of consuming unusually large amounts of food accompanied by a sense of loss of control during the episode.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Binge eating</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01Elz">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Alcohol Problems =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by issues related to the use of alcohol, 
            including dependence, abuse, and the negative physical, psychological, and social consequences resulting from 
            excessive consumption.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Issues related to the use of alcohol, including dependence and abuse.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Alcohol problems</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00mpe">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Pure Obsessions =def. a Distress which is characterized by recurrent and persistent intrusive thoughts, images, 
            or impulses that cause significant distress, without being accompanied by observable compulsive behaviors intended 
            to neutralize them.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Recurrent and persistent intrusive thoughts that cause significant distress, without accompanying compulsive behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pure obsessions</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01Neb">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Impatient Urgency =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a lack of patience and a tendency to act 
            impulsively in urgent situations, often leading to rash decisions and behaviors without consideration for the 
            consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of patience and a tendency to act impulsively in urgent situations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Impatient urgency</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01DAb">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Alcohol Use =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by the consumption of alcoholic beverages, 
            which may lead to problematic use, dependence, or negative physical, psychological, or social consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The consumption of alcoholic beverages, which may lead to problematic use.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Alcohol use</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01wSl">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Restricting =def. an Eating pathology component defined by the deliberate limitation of food intake to influence 
            body weight or shape, typically associated with disordered eating patterns.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component defined by the deliberate limitation of food intake in order to influence body weight or shape, typically associated with disordered eating patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Restricting</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00Fe0">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Negative Relationships =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by relationships that contribute to stress, 
            conflict, or emotional harm, often undermining well-being, personal growth, and the ability to form positive, 
            supportive connections with others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait of negative relationships is that they contribute to stress, conflict, or emotional harm, often undermining well-being and personal growth.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Negative relationships</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P001Y2">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Somatoform =def. a General Psychopathology which is characterized by physical symptoms that cannot be fully explained 
            by a medical condition and reflect psychological distress expressed through somatic complaints.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Somatoform label refers to a category of mental health disorders characterized by physical symptoms that cannot be fully explained by any underlying medical condition, highlighting the complex interaction between mind and body in mental health.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Somatoform</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum may include future expansions or modifications based on emerging research or changes in the understanding of somatoform disorders. 
            It is designed to adapt to new developments by allowing the addition of new related spectra or concepts as needed.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00qSD">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Psychotic =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by symptoms of psychosis, such as delusions, 
            hallucinations, disorganized thinking, or impaired reality testing.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by symptoms of psychosis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Psychotic</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01jKN">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Fatigue =def. a Somatoform which is defined by a persistent or recurrent sense of tiredness, reduced energy, or diminished capacity for sustained physical or mental activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait defined by a persistent or recurrent sense of tiredness, reduced energy, or diminished capacity for sustained physical or mental activity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fatigue</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U007EJ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Antisocial Behavior =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing and Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized 
            by actions that violate societal norms and the rights of others, reflecting a combination of poor impulse control 
            and interpersonal antagonism.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Antisocial Behavior involves actions that violate societal norms and the rights of others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Antisocial Behavior</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C02EBv">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Substance Use =def. a Substance Abuse component which is characterized by the general consumption of alcohol,
            drugs, or other psychoactive substances, without reference to a single substance category, as distinguished
            from substance-specific components such as drug use or alcohol use.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The general consumption of alcohol, drugs, or other psychoactive substances, considered broadly rather than for one specific substance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Substance use</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#hasLevel">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Tags a HiTOP concept (a Tier) with a free-text level name (for example "Spectrum" or "Component") describing the role it plays in one specific factorization. The same concept can carry a different hasLevel value in a different factorization; this property is declared in the core ontology but is only ever asserted inside a factorization's own hierarchy file, never in the core ontology itself. The value is purely descriptive: the actual vertical ordering of a factorization is established by hitop:hasTier alone, not by this property, so no fixed, enumerable set of level names is required in the core ontology.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has Level</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            Previously an object property ordering a fixed set of six core Level subclasses (Factor, Superspectrum, Spectrum, Subfactor, Component, Trait). That fixed ladder required extending the core ontology for every new factorization-specific level combination, which conflicted with the principle that a factorization must not add classes to the shared core. Redeclared as a datatype property so any factorization can freely name a concept's level without touching the core.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00gvD">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Re-experiencing =def. a Distress which is characterized by the involuntary re-experiencing of traumatic events through 
            flashbacks, intrusive memories, or nightmares, often accompanied by intense emotional or physiological reactions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Re-experiencing traumatic events through flashbacks, intrusive memories, or nightmares.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Re-experiencing</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00dc1">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Appetite Gain =def. a Distress which is characterized by an increased desire to eat, often resulting in 
            elevated food intake and potential weight gain, commonly observed in atypical depressive states or in response 
            to emotional distress.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Increased desire to eat, which can lead to weight gain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Appetite gain</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01HGq">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Drug Use =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by the consumption of illicit or prescription drugs, 
            which may lead to problematic use, dependence, or negative physical, psychological, or social consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The consumption of illicit or prescription drugs, which may lead to problematic use.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Drug use</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00D42">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Submissiveness =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a tendency to submit to others and avoid asserting oneself, 
            often resulting in passive behavior, difficulty in standing up for oneself, and a tendency to defer to the wishes or 
            authority of others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to submit to others and avoid asserting oneself.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Submissiveness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01LSp">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Relational Aggression =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by aggression that harms others 
            through manipulation of social relationships, such as spreading rumors, social exclusion, or 
            undermining someone's reputation.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Aggression that harms others through manipulation of social relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Relational aggression</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T019Cj">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Risk Taking =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by engaging in behaviors that involve 
            significant risk, often without regard for potential negative outcomes or consequences, driven by a desire 
            for stimulation or thrill-seeking.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by engaging in behaviors that involve significant risk, often without regard for potential negative outcomes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Risk taking</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00BXK">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Restricted Affectivity =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by limited or constricted emotional expression, 
            often leading to a diminished range of emotional experiences or difficulty in expressing emotions in social or 
            interpersonal contexts.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by limited or constricted emotional expression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Restricted affectivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01PMW">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Dependability =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a lack of reliability and consistency 
            in fulfilling obligations, often resulting in failure to meet commitments or responsibilities, and 
            causing disruptions in personal or professional relationships.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of reliability and consistency in fulfilling obligations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Dependability</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T007eM">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Anxiousness =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a tendency to experience anxiety, nervousness, or unease, 
            often in response to stress or uncertainty, leading to heightened arousal or worry about future events.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to experience anxiety or nervousness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anxiousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01gKP">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Timorousness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing trait characterized by a reduced tendency to be fearful or lacking in confidence, resulting in less hesitation and avoidance in social and achievement-related situations.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a low tendency to be fearful or lacking in confidence, often reflected in reduced shyness and hesitation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Timorousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01GEY">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Marijuana Problems =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by issues related to the use of marijuana, 
            including dependence, abuse, and the negative physical, psychological, and social consequences resulting from 
            excessive consumption.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Issues related to the use of marijuana, including dependence and abuse.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Marijuana problems</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01oMk">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Behavioral avoidance =def. a Fear component or trait which is defined by the consistent tendency to withdraw from or 
            evade situations, thoughts, or stimuli perceived as threatening, distressing, or aversive.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait defined by the consistent tendency to withdraw from or evade situations, thoughts, or stimuli perceived as threatening, distressing, or aversive.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Behavioral avoidance</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T028jy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Emotional detachment =def. a Detachment trait reflecting a persistent lack of emotional responsiveness, warmth, 
            or connection in interpersonal interactions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting a persistent lack of emotional responsiveness, warmth, or connection in interpersonal interactions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Emotional detachment</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C02DSC">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Exhibitionism =def. an Antagonism trait characterized by a recurrent tendency or desire to draw attention to oneself 
            through the display of one’s body, sexuality, or behaviors in ways intended to provoke, shock, or gain validation.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a recurrent tendency or desire to draw attention to oneself through the display of one’s body, sexuality, or behaviors in ways intended to provoke, shock, or gain validation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Exhibitionism</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C022PW">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Sex-related distress =def. a Sexual problems component defined by psychological discomfort, worry, or 
            negative emotional reactions specifically linked to sexual experiences, functioning, or difficulties.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component defined by psychological discomfort, worry, or negative emotional reactions specifically linked to sexual experiences, functioning, or difficulties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sex-related distress</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00cSn">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Appetite Loss =def. a Distress which is characterized by a reduction or loss of desire to eat, 
            often resulting in decreased food intake and potential weight loss, commonly associated with depressive or 
            anxious states.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reduction or loss of desire to eat, which can lead to weight loss.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Appetite loss</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01zXz">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Low sexual desire =def. a Sexual problems component or trait characterized by a persistent or recurrent reduction 
            in interest, motivation, or fantasies related to sexual activity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait characterized by a persistent or recurrent reduction in interest, motivation, or fantasies related to sexual activity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Low sexual desire</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#P003SL">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Thought Disorder =def. a General Psychopathology which is characterized by disorganized thinking, 
            impaired reality testing, and disturbances in the form or content of thought, reflecting severe cognitive and 
            perceptual disruptions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Thought Disorder refers to a category of mental health conditions characterized by disorganized thinking, impaired reality testing, and disturbances in the form or content of thought.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Thought Disorder</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This spectrum allows for the integration of additional related spectra or concepts as new insights into thought disorders emerge. 
            It is structured to adapt to evolving understandings and classifications within the domain of cognitive and thought-related disturbances.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00sWr">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Inexpressivity =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by a lack of emotional expression, including reduced 
            facial expressions, vocal inflection, and gestures, often observed as a negative symptom in psychotic disorders.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by a lack of emotional expression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Inexpressivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00e0L">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Wellbeing =def. a Distress which is characterized by a diminished state of mental and physical health, 
            reflected in reduced happiness, life satisfaction, or emotional balance.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A low level of mental and physical wellbeing, characterized by reduced feelings of happiness, contentment, and overall health.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Wellbeing</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#V1052k">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#0004KV"/>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">The HiTOP ontology version 1.0 represents the foundational structure of the Hierarchical Taxonomy of Psychopathology. It encodes empirically-derived components, syndromes, and spectra to address limitations of traditional classifications such as DSM-5 and ICD-11. This version supports dimensional, hierarchical representation of psychopathology, reduces diagnostic overlap and heterogeneity, and is intended for both clinical and research use.</dcterms:description>
    <dcterms:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-08-30</dcterms:issued>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HiTOP Core Ontology Version 1.0</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1.0</owl:versionInfo>
  </owl:NamedIndividual>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T0177S">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Theft =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by a tendency to steal or engage in dishonest 
            acquisition of property, often driven by impulsivity, disregard for social norms, or a lack of remorse.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to steal or engage in dishonest acquisition of property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Theft</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01MjB">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Fraud =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by deceptive behavior intended to secure unfair or 
            unlawful gain, often involving manipulation, dishonesty, or the misrepresentation of information to deceive others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Deceptive behavior intended to secure unfair or unlawful gain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fraud</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01Ziz">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Deceitfulness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a tendency to lie, cheat, 
            or deceive others, often for personal gain, manipulation, or to avoid negative consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to lie, cheat, or deceive others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deceitfulness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/iaoIAO_0000115"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00416">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Head Pain =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by headaches or other forms of head pain that are not 
            fully attributable to identifiable medical causes, reflecting the expression of psychological distress 
            through somatic symptoms.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component related to headaches or other types of head pain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Head Pain</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00yfU">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Depressivity =def. a Detachment which is characterized by persistent feelings of sadness, hopelessness, and 
            emotional pain, often accompanied by a diminished interest in life and a negative view of the self.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by feelings of sadness and hopelessness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Depressivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01hQc">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Anhedonia =def. a Detachment which is conceptualized as a stable, enduring disposition toward diminished pleasure or 
            interest in typically rewarding experiences, leading to a reduced ability to experience joy or satisfaction from activities that are usually enjoyable.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Anhedonia conceptualized as a Trait refers to a stable, enduring disposition toward diminished pleasure or interest in typically rewarding experiences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anhedonia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01KXo">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Destructive Aggression =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by aggression that results in 
            damage to property or the environment, often reflecting a disregard for social norms, authority, or 
            the consequences of one’s actions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Aggression that results in damage to property or the environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Destructive aggression</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T011K6">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Withdrawal =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a tendency to retreat from social interactions and avoid 
            engagement with others, often reflecting discomfort with social closeness or reduced motivation for 
            interpersonal connection.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to retreat from social interactions and avoid engagement with others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Withdrawal</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00ZyP">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Suicidality =def. a Distress which is characterized by the presence of thoughts, intentions, or behaviors 
            related to ending one’s own life, often associated with severe emotional suffering and hopelessness.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The presence of thoughts or behaviors related to suicide.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Suicidality</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01eG6">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Dominance =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a desire to control or lead others, 
            often displaying assertiveness, power, and a tendency to assert one's will over others in social or 
            organizational contexts.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a desire to control or lead others, often displaying assertiveness and power.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dominance</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01BfQ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Ruminative Deliberation =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing trait characterized by a reduced tendency to engage in prolonged and repetitive deliberation about potential decisions and their outcomes.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a low tendency toward excessive and repetitive thinking about potential decisions and their outcomes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Ruminative deliberation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01l9M">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Cardiopulmonary =def. a Somatoform which is defined by signs or symptoms involving the heart and lungs, 
            such as circulatory, respiratory, or exercise-related difficulties.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait associated with signs or symptoms involving the heart and lungs, such as circulatory, respiratory, or exercise-related difficulties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cardiopulmonary</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T012QL">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Interpersonal Passivity =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a lack of initiative or assertiveness in 
            social interactions, often manifesting as submissiveness, indecision, or reluctance to express personal needs 
            or preferences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of initiative or assertiveness in social interactions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interpersonal passivity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00oKM">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Hyperactive Cognition =def. a Mania which is characterized by increased cognitive activity, including racing thoughts, 
            distractibility, and accelerated ideation, often leading to difficulties in concentration and goal-directed thinking.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Increased cognitive activity, often characterized by racing thoughts and distractibility.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hyperactive cognition</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01T3u">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Honesty =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a tendency to be deceitful or untruthful, 
            often involving the manipulation of others or a disregard for truthfulness in social interactions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait marked by a tendency to be deceitful or untruthful.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Honesty</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00Mpl">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Enclosed Spaces =def. a Fear which is characterized by fear or anxiety related to confined or small spaces, 
            often involving concerns about restriction, suffocation, or inability to escape.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear or anxiety related to confined or small spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Enclosed spaces</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01nVp">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Anger/irritability =def. a Distress component or trait which is defined by a heightened propensity toward frustration, 
            hostility, or easily provoked emotional reactivity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component or trait characterized by a heightened propensity toward frustration, hostility, or easily provoked emotional reactivity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anger/irritability</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00JTU">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Interactive Anxiety =def. a Fear which is characterized by anxiety experienced in social interactions and 
            group settings, often involving concerns about being judged, embarrassed, or negatively evaluated by others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Anxiety experienced in social interactions and group settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interactive anxiety</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01xzj">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Muscle building =def. an Eating pathology component involving persistent efforts to increase muscularity through 
            exercise, diet, or supplementation, sometimes associated with body image concerns.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component involving persistent efforts to increase muscularity through exercise, diet, or supplementation, sometimes associated with body image concerns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Muscle building</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C020XA">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Difficulties with arousal =def. a Sexual problems component characterized by challenges in attaining or 
            maintaining adequate sexual excitement or physiological arousal during sexual activity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component defined by challenges in attaining or maintaining adequate sexual excitement or physiological arousal during sexual activity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Difficulties with arousal</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01QNN">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Alienation =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a sense of estrangement or detachment from others, 
            often leading to feelings of social isolation, loneliness, and a lack of connection to social groups or 
            society at large.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting a sense of estrangement or detachment from others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Alienation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T010c6">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Suspiciousness =def. a Detachment which is characterized by a tendency to be distrustful and suspicious of others, 
            often involving beliefs that others have harmful intentions or cannot be relied upon.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to be distrustful and suspicious of others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Suspiciousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00Cgy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Separation Insecurity =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by anxiety and insecurity in response to 
            separation from significant others, often leading to clinginess, fear of abandonment, and difficulty coping with 
            distance or changes in relationships.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by anxiety and insecurity in response to separation from significant others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Separation insecurity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C02CiQ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Destruction of property =def. an Antisocial behavior component involving deliberate or impulsive damage, vandalism, 
            or destruction of objects, possessions, or physical environments.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component involving deliberate or impulsive damage, vandalism, or destruction of objects, possessions, or physical environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Destruction of property</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01yno">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Negative attitudes toward obesity =def. an Eating pathology trait reflecting unfavorable beliefs, stereotypes, or 
            stigmatizing attitudes toward individuals with obesity, often linked to social or cultural biases.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting unfavorable beliefs, stereotypes, or stigmatizing attitudes toward individuals with obesity, often linked to social or cultural biases.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Negative attitudes toward obesity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00rnS">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Disorganized =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by disorganized thinking and behavior, 
            including incoherent speech, erratic actions, and difficulties maintaining goal-directed activity.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by disorganized thinking and behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Disorganized</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C025ex">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Health/Illness anxiety =def. a Somatoform and Distress component characterized by excessive worry or preoccupation 
            with having, developing, or misinterpreting symptoms of a serious medical condition.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by excessive worry or preoccupation with having, developing, or misinterpreting symptoms of a serious medical condition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Health/Illness anxiety</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01qTa">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            BII phobia =def. a Fear component which is defined by marked fear or avoidance of situations involving blood, injury, 
            or invasive medical procedures, often accompanied by physiological reactions such as fainting.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by marked fear or avoidance of situations involving blood, injury, or invasive medical procedures, often associated with physiological reactions such as fainting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BII phobia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C0033z">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Malaise =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by a general feeling of discomfort, unease, or lack of well-being, 
            reflecting psychological distress manifesting as nonspecific physical symptoms.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component related to general discomfort or unease.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Malaise</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00wk6">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Unusual Beliefs and Experiences =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by the presence of atypical beliefs 
            and perceptual experiences, such as magical thinking, perceptual distortions, or ideas of reference, that deviate 
            from cultural norms.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by the presence of atypical beliefs and experiences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Unusual beliefs and experiences</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01W1E">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Excitement Seeking =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a desire for new, thrilling, 
            or risky experiences, often driving individuals to engage in activities that provide immediate gratification 
            or stimulation, regardless of potential consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a desire for new, thrilling, or risky experiences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Excitement seeking</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01FDy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Marijuana Use =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by the consumption of marijuana, 
            which may lead to problematic use, dependence, or negative physical, psychological, or social consequences.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The consumption of marijuana, which may lead to problematic use.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Marijuana use</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00Urw">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Checking =def. a Fear which is characterized by compulsive behaviors involving repeated checking of objects or 
            situations—such as locks, appliances, or personal belongings—typically performed to reduce anxiety about 
            potential harm or danger.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Compulsive checking behaviors, such as repeatedly checking locks or appliances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Checking</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01OY2">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            (low) Planful Control =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a poor ability to plan and execute 
            tasks effectively, often resulting in impulsive actions, disorganization, and an inability to meet goals 
            or manage responsibilities.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait indicating poor ability to plan and execute tasks effectively.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">(low) Planful control</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00TgL">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Rituals =def. a Fear which is characterized by compulsive behaviors or mental acts performed in a specific and 
            repetitive manner, typically intended to prevent feared outcomes or reduce anxiety.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Compulsive rituals or behaviors performed in a specific manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rituals</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01SYW">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Blame Externalization =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by a tendency to attribute failures or 
            problems to external factors, such as other people, circumstances, or societal influences, rather than 
            recognizing internal causes or personal responsibility.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to attribute failures or problems to external factors rather than internal ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Blame externalization</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C0277d">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Reality distortion =def. a Thought disorder component characterized by alterations in the perception or 
            interpretation of reality, such as delusions, hallucinations, or disorganized thinking.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by alterations in the perception or interpretation of reality, such as delusions, hallucinations, or disorganized thinking.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Reality distortion</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T0094I">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Hostility =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a tendency toward aggression, antagonism, or ill will 
            towards others, often accompanied by a deep-seated mistrust or negative attitudes, leading to interpersonal conflict.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency toward aggression or antagonism.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hostility</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C02FZY">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Substance Problems =def. a Substance Abuse component which is characterized by dependence, abuse, or negative
            physical, psychological, or social consequences resulting from substance use in general, without reference
            to a single substance category.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Dependence, abuse, or negative consequences resulting from substance use, considered broadly rather than for one specific substance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Substance problems</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00hPJ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Avoidance =def. a Distress which is characterized by efforts to avoid thoughts, feelings, people, places, 
            or situations that are associated with traumatic experiences or stress, often as a means of reducing 
            emotional discomfort or fear.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Efforts to avoid reminders or situations that are associated with traumatic experiences or stress.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Avoidance</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00jw5">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Numbing =def. a Distress which is characterized by emotional numbness or detachment from feelings, 
            typically as a psychological response to overwhelming stress or trauma, and often accompanied by 
            a diminished capacity to experience positive emotions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Emotional numbness or detachment from feelings as a response to overwhelming stress or trauma.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Numbing</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00vjR">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Cognitive Perceptual Dysregulation =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by disturbances in cognition and 
            perception, including unusual beliefs, perceptual aberrations, and difficulties distinguishing internal thoughts 
            from external reality.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by disturbances in cognition and perception.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cognitive perceptual dysregulation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00OuR">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Situational Phobia =def. a Fear which is characterized by fear or anxiety related to specific situations 
            or environments, such as flying, driving, tunnels, or elevators, typically leading to avoidance or marked distress.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear or anxiety related to specific situations or environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Situational phobia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00N4I">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Animal Phobia =def. a Fear which is characterized by fear or anxiety related to animals, 
            often involving specific triggers such as dogs, insects, or snakes, and resulting in avoidance behavior or 
            intense distress upon exposure.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fear or anxiety related to animals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Animal phobia</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00tUQ">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Avolition =def. a Thought Disorder which is characterized by a lack of motivation to initiate and sustain purposeful 
            activities, often resulting in reduced goal-directed behavior and functional impairment in daily life.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by a lack of motivation to initiate and sustain purposeful activities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Avolition</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01a7u">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Grandiosity =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by an exaggerated sense of one’s own importance, 
            abilities, or achievements, often accompanied by a lack of consideration for others and a belief in one's superiority 
            or entitlement.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by an exaggerated sense of one's own importance, abilities, or achievements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Grandiosity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01fc8">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Flirtatiousness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by behavior that seeks to attract 
            romantic or sexual interest from others through playful, suggestive, or provocative means, often involving charm 
            or manipulation.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by behavior that seeks to attract romantic or sexual interest from others through playful or provocative means.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Flirtatiousness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01d9I">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Egocentricity =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by an excessive focus on oneself 
            and one’s own needs and desires, often leading to a lack of consideration for others and a diminished capacity 
            for empathy or understanding of different perspectives.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by an excessive focus on oneself and one's own needs and desires.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Egocentricity</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C006MD">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Cognitive =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by cognitive symptoms or dysfunctions such as difficulties 
            with memory, attention, or concentration, that are not fully explained by medical or neurological conditions, 
            reflecting psychological distress manifesting in cognitive domains.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component related to cognitive symptoms and dysfunctions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cognitive</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01vT5">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Excessive exercise =def. an Eating pathology component defined by compulsive or disproportionate physical activity, 
            often performed to control weight, shape, or mood, despite potential health risks.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component characterized by compulsive or disproportionate physical activity, often performed with the aim of controlling weight, shape, or mood, despite potential health risks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Excessive exercise</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00nyb">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Euphoric Activation =def. a Mania which is characterized by heightened mood, increased energy, and elevated 
            self-confidence, often associated with euphoric or expansive affect seen in manic or hypomanic episodes.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state of heightened mood and increased energy, often associated with mania or hypomania.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Euphoric activation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/rightsHolder"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00HCy">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Ineptitude =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by a lack of skill, competence, or ability in performing tasks 
            or handling situations, often resulting in difficulties in achieving goals or completing responsibilities.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a lack of skill or competence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ineptitude</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T00A0Z">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Perseveration =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by the repetition of a particular response or 
            behavior despite the absence or cessation of a stimulus, often resulting in difficulty shifting attention or 
            adapting to changing situations.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by the repetition of a particular response despite the absence or cessation of a stimulus.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Perseveration</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#U004dm">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Distress =def. an Internalizing which is characterized by significant emotional suffering or discomfort, 
            often involving persistent negative affect such as sadness, hopelessness, or irritability.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Distress involves significant emotional suffering or discomfort.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Distress</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            This subfactor is designed to be adaptable to future updates and expansions. 
            It allows for the incorporation of new elements or modifications to existing components as research advances and 
            our understanding of psychological phenomena evolves.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00KL0">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Performance Anxiety =def. a Fear which is characterized by anxiety related to performing tasks or activities, 
            particularly in public or under observation, often driven by fear of failure, embarrassment, or negative evaluation.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Anxiety related to performing tasks or activities, often in public or under observation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Performance anxiety</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00WJc">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Lassitude =def. a Distress which is characterized by physical or mental weariness and a lack of energy, 
            often accompanied by reduced motivation, sluggishness, or difficulty initiating tasks.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state of physical or mental weariness and lack of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lassitude</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/date"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00217">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Somatization =def. a Somatoform which is characterized by the expression of psychological distress through multiple, 
            recurrent physical symptoms that cannot be fully explained by medical conditions.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component involving the expression of psychological distress through physical symptoms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Somatization</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00kEN">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Dissociation =def. a Distress which is characterized by a mental process used to cope with stress or trauma, 
            leading to a sense of detachment from one’s surroundings, identity, or sense of self, and often resulting in 
            altered perception or memory.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mental process used to cope with stress or trauma, leading to a sense of detachment from one's surroundings or self.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dissociation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01JH8">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Physical Aggression =def. an Antisocial Behavior which is characterized by the use of physical acts of 
            violence towards others, often involving harm or the threat of harm, and typically reflecting a disregard for 
            social norms and the rights of others.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Aggression involving physical acts of violence towards others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Physical aggression</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01tAk">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Cognitive restraint =def. an Eating pathology trait which is defined by the deliberate control or restriction of 
            eating behavior based on cognitive rules or beliefs about food, body weight, or dieting.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait reflecting the deliberate control or restriction of eating behavior based on cognitive rules or beliefs about food, body weight, or dieting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cognitive restraint</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C01Ip4">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Drug Problems =def. a Harmful Substance Abuse which is characterized by issues related to the use of drugs, 
            including dependence, abuse, and the negative physical, psychological, and social consequences resulting from 
            excessive or harmful consumption.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Issues related to the use of drugs, including dependence and abuse.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Drug problems</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T01bz7">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Manipulativeness =def. an Antagonistic Externalizing which is characterized by a tendency to control or 
            influence others for personal gain, often in a devious or underhanded manner, without regard for others' well-being or 
            autonomy.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by a tendency to control or influence others for personal gain, often in a devious manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Manipulativeness</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#T018ir">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Distractibility =def. a Disinhibited Externalizing which is characterized by an inability to maintain focus, 
            leading to frequent shifts in attention, impulsive responses to external stimuli, and difficulty completing tasks.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A trait characterized by an inability to maintain focus, leading to frequent shifts in attention.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Distractibility</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#C00aMF">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <iao:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">
            Agitation =def. a Distress which is characterized by a state of heightened emotional or physiological arousal, 
            often resulting in restlessness, irritability, or erratic behavior.
        </iao:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">State of being overly excited or disturbed, often resulting in restlessness or erratic behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Agitation</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/license"/>
  <owl:AnnotationProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/isVersionOf"/>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP">
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="N0c50fa2f4b0c47b2aa6afd0c30d9db72">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#hasTier"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A structural component of the HiTOP taxonomy used to define horizontal relationships within a specific level of the hierarchy. Each instance of Tier represents a distinct grouping or division within a given Level, encompassing constructs such as clusters, categories, or subcategories. The restriction ensures that all instances of this class must have at least one tier (via the property hitop:hasTier) that is also an instance of this class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tier</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#hasTier">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.org/hitop#O002sP"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Establishes the concrete parent-child relationship between two HiTOP concepts within one factorization, for example Internalizing hasTier Anxiousness. Declared in the core ontology but only ever asserted inside a factorization's own hierarchy file, never in the core ontology itself. This relationship alone determines the vertical ordering of a factorization tree: a child is always exactly one step narrower than its parent, so no separate rank or Level class hierarchy is required to keep a factorization internally ordered.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has Tier</rdfs:label>
    <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">
            Indicates the potential for future inclusion of additional tiers or modification of existing ones to reflect new developments within specific levels of the hierarchy.
            Supports flexibility in expanding or refining the taxonomy based on emerging research and evolving understanding of horizontal relationships among psychological constructs.
        </skos:changeNote>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/hitop#0004KV">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This class represents a version entity used to document the version number and descriptive information related to the evolution of HiTOP ontology elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Version</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
</rdf:RDF>
